# One `@` parameter the pointee check asks about (panel 103): the extern's
# C name, the parameter's written name and position, the declared type as
# C, and the `.hero` line the verdict must land on. A record of its own so
# that the file that asks (`cli/pointee.hero`) and the file that writes and
# reads the units (`cli/header_types.hero`) can both name it without either
# importing the other — Heroes refuses module cycles, and the seam between
# asking and reading is the one worth keeping.
#
# `declared` is a C type for a width ask, `ptr` or `handle` for a depth ask,
# and one of the words below for the asks a LEND makes (panel 194's R7,
# defects 092 and 395; defect 411): what unit C counts a `counted_by`
# parameter in, whether a whole record lent with `@` and no count reaches a
# `void *`, and whether a `cstr`'s pointer points at `const` bytes, with the
# count of parameters it is asked under.
record Pointee
    name: str
    param: str
    index: i64
    declared: str
    file: str
    line: i64
    depth: bool

# A parameter declared `counted_by`: the header's type for it, whose pointee
# is the unit its count is compared in (`emit/lend_extent.hero`).
constant UNIT: str
    "unit"

# A group's record lent whole through `@` with no `counted_by`: refused where
# the header takes it as `void *`, since nothing then bounds what C reaches.
constant WHOLE: str
    "whole"

# A `cstr` parameter that is not `@`: what `s.cstr()`, a lease or a literal
# lends it is read-only, so the header's pointer must point at `const` bytes
# (defect 411, `emit/ffi_read_only.hero`).
constant READ: str
    "read"

# How many parameters the declaration gives, in `index`, asked of a function
# with a `READ` ask: its parameters stand for the header's only where the two
# counts agree (`emit/ffi_read_only.hero`).
constant ARITY: str
    "arity"

# The same ask once the header has answered: what its parameter points at,
# as the header's own type text (`size_t`, `void`, `struct opaque`). Built by
# `cli/header_types.hero` from the dump and handed to `emit/ffi.hero`'s
# `explain`, because one class of failure names the TYPE and not the
# parameter — clang says `incomplete type 'struct opaque'` and nothing else
# (defect 010, 2026-09-04) — so the reader has to find the parameter from
# the type, and only the asker knows which parameter was asked about which.
#
# For a lend's three asks it is the parameter's own type, whole (`int *`,
# `LPVOID`), since a pointer the header spells through a typedef has no `*`
# to cut at; `pointee` is what it points at read through every typedef, which
# is the name clang gives an incomplete one, and empty for every other ask.
record Answered
    asked: Pointee
    header_type: str
    pointee: str
